    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and it passes along with the full build.\n\nDone. The change is implemented cleanly:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field with proper API documentation. Keeping it in the schema is the right place since DTOs here are generated from the spec.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a single `@Mapping` on the existing `toOwnerDto(Owner)` method that computes `displayName` as `\"LastName, FirstName\"` from the stored names. This reuses the one mapping already responsible for entity\u2192DTO conversion, so every endpoint returning an owner (create, get, update, list) gets the formatted name consistently \u2014 no new class or duplicated formatting logic.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreComputesDisplayName`) and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
